Example of using Fenix for online process recovery.
Generates an artificial failure to demonstrate recovery.

Input files
in.memory   : Checkpoints to memory (using Fenix's buddy-rank checkpointing)
in.file     : Checkpoints to file, uses Fenix only for online recovery
              Note: in.file requires line 45 to be uncommented for restart files
               to actually be written

Relevant Variables
nspare      : How many spare ranks to allocate
fail_rank   : Which rank(s) to generate failures on
x, y, z     : Input region size in each dimension (x20)
